I. Adding the meta-got layer to your build
=================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-got'

II. Misc
========

--- replace with specific information about the meta-got layer ---

Add local.conf.sample and bblayer.bb.sample to meta-got/conf/templates. It will be the files used in build.
Then add it to TEMPLATCONF acordding to the machine:
TEMPLATECONF=../../../layers/meta-got/conf/templates/default/ source init-build-env 
 source init-build-env 

TEMPLATECONF=/home/gotardo/Dev/Projects/got-target/layers/meta-got/conf/templates/default
TEMPLATECONF=/home/gotardo/Dev/Projects/got-target/layers/meta-got/conf/templates/qemu
TEMPLATECONF=/home/gotardo/Dev/Projects/got-target/layers/meta-got/conf/templates/rpi3
source layers/openembedded-core/oe-init-build-env
source ../layers/openembedded-core/oe-init-build-env

runqemu qemux86-64 snapshot nographic